Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1789937999999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789862399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The window high 2771.00 (1787270400000) is 25 bars old and untouched; price is still below the 2680.00 range high on a closing basis, so the breakout leg remains an attempt inside the range, not accepted structure.", "The last bar was rejected at 2700.00, leaving an upper tail of about 67 points, and the prior 2680.00 attempt (1789084800000) closed roughly 165 points below its high; the same zone has produced two visible sellers' reactions, an incipient double top.", "1789430400000 is a wide bear bar (open 2513.91, low 2358.62, close 2397.10) that erased several bull closes in one bar, showing two-sided trade with bears still able to produce strong bars inside the range.", "A 29-bar overlapping range after a near-vertical spike is equally consistent with a climactic spike followed by distribution; the spike's 2771.00 tail bar closed only at 2515.30, well below its high."], "evidence_for": ["The most recent close 2632.98 is the highest close of the supplied 120 bars, and the last two bars are consecutive bull bars that take out the prior six bars' highs and the 2557.46 inner ceiling.", "Whole-window structure is a bull sequence of higher swing lows (1368.42 -> 1512.91 -> 1551.60 -> 1694.74 -> 2357.18) with the 2358.62 low (1789430400000) holding above 2357.18, so the 29-bar sideways stretch follows a strong bull spike and reads as a bull flag rather than a completed top.", "Range pullbacks have been shallow relative to the 1905.63-2771.00 spike: most range closes stay above the spike's midpoint near 2338, and each push down to the 2357-2395 area has been bought back into the 2440-2530 zone.", "Each successive upper test has closed higher (2514.72 at 1789084800000 versus 2632.98 at 1789776000000), i.e. sellers at 2680-2700 have not produced a lower close or an accepted break back down."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars, first open 2066.43 (1779494400000), last bar open 2612.03 / high 2700 / low 2604.75 / close 2632.98 (close_time_ms 1789862399999).", "Bars 1-15 of the window decline from high 2143.61 (1779494400000) to low 1368.42 (1780704000000); the 1780704000000 bar has range 1368.42-1599.27 and closes 1568.55 in the upper part of that range with a long lower tail.", "Higher lows follow the 1368.42 low: 1512.91 (1782432000000), 1551.60 (1782777600000), 1694.74 (1783296000000); rising highs reach 1959.37 (1785024000000), then ~12 bars overlap between roughly 1820 and 1960 (1785456000000-1787011200000).", "Three-bar bull spike from 1905.63 to 2771.00: opens/closes 1916.51/2252.16, 2252.20/2326.32, 2326.31/2515.30 at 1787097600000, 1787184000000, 1787270400000; the 2771.00 high leaves a large upper tail on the third bar.", "Since 1787356800000 the market has been sideways: 29 bars between low 2357.18 (1788307200000) and spike highs 2680.00 (1789084800000) and 2700.00 (1789776000000), with most closes between roughly 2390 and 2540 and an inner ceiling at 2557.46 (1787788800000).", "Two separate upside spike attempts above that inner ceiling: 1789084800000 (open 2436.83, high 2680.00, close 2514.72, upper tail ~165) and 1789689600000-1789776000000 (close 2612.02, then high 2700.00 with close 2632.98, upper tail ~67).", "1789430400000 is a large bear bar inside the same range: open 2513.91, low 2358.62, close 2397.10, i.e. a wide body closing near its low.", "The last close 2632.98 is the highest close in the supplied 120-bar window, and the 2700.00 high is still below the window high 2771.00."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear leg of the window: 15 bars of lower highs and lower lows from 2143.61 into an accelerating sell-off that reaches 1368.42 (1780704000000), where the bar closes at 1568.55 in the upper 72% of its 1368.42-1599.27 range, a long-lower-tail reversal bar.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779494400000, "upper_boundary": "2143.61"}, {"description": "Recovery and uptrend from the 1368.42 low: higher lows at 1512.91 (1782432000000) and 1551.60 (1782777600000) with rising highs into 1959.37 (1785024000000), followed by an overlapping ~1820-1960 pause (1785456000000-1787011200000) that holds well above the 1368.42 origin.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1959.37"}, {"description": "Three-bar bull spike: bars at 1787097600000, 1787184000000 and 1787270400000 run from 1905.63 to 2771.00 with closes 2252.16, 2326.32 and 2515.30; the 2771.00 extreme is a spike high with a large upper tail and has not been retested.", "end_time_ms": 1787270400000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Trading range after the spike: 29 bars from 1787356800000 to the last bar, bounded by 2357.18 (1788307200000) and the 2680.00 spike high (1789084800000), with heavy overlap, most closes between roughly 2390 and 2540, and an inner ceiling near 2557.46 (1787788800000).", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Two upside spike attempts into the same 2680.00-2700.00 area (1789084800000: high 2680.00, close 2514.72; 1789776000000: high 2700.00, close 2632.98) separated by a sell-off to 2358.62 (1789430400000). The pair is a possible double top at the range high, though the second attempt closes 118 points higher than the first.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789084800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Two-bar bull leg / breakout attempt: 1789689600000 (open 2446.22, high 2643.52, close 2612.02) and 1789776000000 (open 2612.03, high 2700.00, low 2604.75, close 2632.98). Price lifts above the 2557.46 inner ceiling and prints the window's highest close, but has not yet closed above the 2680.00 range high.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Acceptance above the 2680.00 range high, e.g. a close above it followed by another bar closing above 2700.00, would confirm the range breakout and support the bull-trend / breakout-spike read.", "A close back below 2557.46 and into the 2390-2540 range body would negate the breakout attempt and restore an intact trading range between 2357.18 and 2680.00.", "A close below 2357.18 would be a bear breakout from the 29-bar range and would shift the structural read away from the bull flag toward a bear or transition classification.", "Failure to exceed 2680.00 over the next few bars while forming a lower high below 2700.00 would leave the two-sided/double-top interpretation as the strongest alternative and reduce Always-In relevance to low."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789934399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Since the 2358.62 retest (bar 90) the market printed higher highs (2609.02 to 2643.52 to 2700) and higher lows (2358.62 to 2436.87 to 2568.16): a 23-bar advance of about +14.5% from the low.", "The pullback low 2568.16 (bar 118) held 30.59 above the 2537.57 top of the 47-bar middle block - the classic hold above the breakout point after a range breakout.", "Bars 107-108 were large bull trend bars (bodies +71.45 and +56.31, closes at 92% and 89% of range) and the resumption bars 119-120 again closed at/above the upper part of their ranges (100% and 65%).", "A 50% retracement is normal for a bull channel pullback; the current one held above the last higher low (2436.87) and price has already recovered about half of it."], "evidence_for": ["Three separate upside probes inside the window ended in full or partial failure: 2509.15/2537.57 (bars 17-22) reversed to 2436.73 within one bar (bar 23); 2680 (bar 65) reversed to 2358.62 (bar 90); 2700 (bar 112) closed at 20.5% of its range and gave back 131.84 points in six bars.", "The 120-bar range is 342.82 points wide and the middle 47 bars (18-64) closed only between 2436.73 and 2537.57, a large overlapping block rather than a trending sequence.", "The 2700 breakout is not accepted: the pullback to 2568.16 (bar 118) traded back below 2609.02 (bar 85 high) and below 2643.52 (bar 108 high), and the last close 2631.93 is still 68.07 under the window high.", "The push into 2700 came from four overlapping bars with ranges of 20.63-29.66 points (bars 109-112) plus one spike-and-fail bar, channel/wedge behaviour rather than spike-and-follow-through."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars, 1788206400000 to 1789934399999. Window open 2479.65, last close 2631.93 (+6.1%); window low 2357.18 (bar 10), window high 2700 (bar 112), midpoint 2528.59; total range 342.82 points (14.5% of the low).", "Last two bars resume up: bar 119 opened 2577.69 and closed at its high 2611.00 (range 39.52); bar 120 opened 2611.00, high 2645.88, low 2605.96, close 2631.93, i.e. 13.95 under its high and 65% of its range.", "Before that, six bars (bars 113-118) declined from bar 114 high 2658.79 to bar 118 low 2568.16; bar 116 was a 63.18-point bear bar closing 2586.68 in the lower quarter of its range.", "Bar 112 spiked to 2700, above the earlier spike high 2680 (bar 65), but closed 2638.49, only 20.5% of its 77.33-point range; the pullback from 2700 to 2568.16 retraced 131.84 points, essentially 50% of the 2436.87 (bar 104 low) to 2700 advance.", "Bars 107-108 are the strongest bull bars of the recent leg: bodies +71.45 and +56.31, closes at 92% and 89% of their ranges; they cleared 2537.57, the high of the ~47-bar middle block (bars 18-64).", "Bar 65 was a single-bar spike from 2457.12 to 2680 (range 235.81, close 2555.52 at 47% of range); the following decline retraced the whole move to 2358.62 (bar 90), only 1.44 points (0.06%) above the window low 2357.18.", "Recurring window pattern: strong spike bars followed by full or near-full retracement. Bar 17 (2407.48 to 2506.79, close 97.7% of range) was given back by bar 23 (2527.18 high to 2436.73 low, close 2450.96); bar 85 spiked to 2609.02 but closed 2514.07 (1.3% of a 96.21 range) and led to 2358.62.", "From the 2358.62 low the lows step up 2436.87 (bar 104) then 2568.16 (bar 118), and the highs step up 2643.52 (bar 108) then 2700 (bar 112); the 2568.16 pullback low held 30.59 above the 2537.57 middle-block high.", "The advance into 2700 was four overlapping small bars (bars 109-112 ranges 29.66, 23.94, 20.63, then the 77.33 spike-and-fail of bar 112), channel-like rather than a spike sequence.", "Always-In is long on the recent sequence (from the 2568.16 low / bar 104 low up-leg), but relevance is reduced because the 2700 probe failed, price is still 68.07 below the window high, and two earlier spikes in this window were fully retraced."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Whole-window two-sided range: 2357.18 (bar 10 low) to 2700 (bar 112 high), 342.82 points; midpoint 2528.59; last close 2631.93 sits in the upper quarter. Three upside probes stalled or failed inside it: 2509.15/2537.57 (bars 17/22), 2680 (bar 65), 2700 (bar 112).", "end_time_ms": 1789934399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1788206400000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Long middle block, ~47 bars (bars 18-64): highest high 2537.57 (bar 22), most lows 2436-2442 (bar 23 low 2436.73, bar 47 low 2441.33) with one dip to 2411.04 (bar 59); heavy bar-to-bar overlap and no sustained closes outside. This block is the breakout reference the last 14 bars cleared.", "end_time_ms": 1789127999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2436.73", "start_time_ms": 1788451200000, "upper_boundary": "2537.57"}, {"description": "Buy-climax spike bar 65: 2457.12 to 2680 in one 235.81-point bar, close 2555.52; the following decline retraced the entire advance and slightly undercut to 2358.62 (bar 90), a 0.06% retest of the window low 2357.18 (double bottom).", "end_time_ms": 1789516799999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789128000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Recent bull leg: low 2436.87 (bar 104), spike bars 107-108 (bodies +71.45, +56.31, closes near highs), then four overlapping small bars into the 2700 high (bar 112, weak close), then a 131.84-point (about 50%) pullback to 2568.16 (bar 118) and a two-bar resumption (bar 119 close = high 2611.00; bar 120 close 2631.93).", "end_time_ms": 1789934399999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Potential top pattern, unconfirmed: bar 112 makes a marginal new high 2700 over the 2680 spike but closes at 2638.49 (lower quarter of range), then bars 113-118 break below the 2578.44 low of the bar-108 breakout bar and retrace to 2568.16. It is not a confirmed reversal while 2568.16 holds and bars 119-120 close back in the upper half of the pullback.", "end_time_ms": 1789934399999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2568.16", "start_time_ms": 1789804800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull-trend shift: a close above 2700 (bar 112 high) followed by a pullback 